ely.\")],\n \"src/audit/recorder.ts:35\",'subject: z.object({ kind: z.enum([\"patient\", \"staff\", \"system\"]), id: z.string() }),',\n \"Searched for audit writers that omit subject or overwrite agent ids; every writer spreads identity() and sets subject, which is required by the schema.\",\n \"Subject is a required separate field. Whether SMS subject is verified is judged in A01.3.\")\nno(\"A01.2\",\"src/integrations/payments.ts:33\",\"authorization: `Bearer ${await key(clinicId)}`,\",\"Payments and SMS (sms.ts:34) use static per-clinic provider keys from Secrets Manager, not short-lived credentials carrying agent identity or delegation. EHR (ehr-mcp.ts:41) mints tokens from a static client secret.\")\nno(\"A01.3\",\"src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:52\",'req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");',\"SMS signature failure is logged and the request continues, so the subject phone:<from> comes from an unverified payload. Webchat subject is a verified JWT sub (webchat.ts:50) but is not carried into tool credentials.\")\nno(\"A02.2\",\"src/workers/reminders.ts:49\",'log.warn({ clinic: clinic.id, scope: err.scope }, \"reminders halted\");',\"Halted reminders path logs and breaks with no audit record. Pre-run refusals (webchat.ts:36 invalid token, 404s, SMS 400/404) also write no audit record.\")\nno(\"A02.4\",\"src/routes/webchat.ts:43\",'const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;',\"Tenant for the run and audit records comes from the caller's x-clinic-id header ahead of the verified JWT claim. executor.ts:63 also takes clinicId from model input.\")\nno(\"A03.1\",\"src/agent/identity.ts:24\",'.filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))',\"Only .txt prompts are hashed, so prompts/system.md (the system prompt, loop.ts:13) is not in the agent-type-id.\")\nno(\"A03.2\",\"src/agent/identity.ts:24\",'.filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))',\"Extension filter skips prompts/system.md. Config list is a