{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDjegVcJdjUxNRp4cdKT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed R14, A01, A02, A03 and A04 and saved the result in `agent/brace-findings.json`. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch R14,A01,A02,A03,A04 --before-challenges` passes: 4 gaps and 1 na_candidate. I ran no challenges and added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| A01 | gap | The agent has its own IAM role and service account. But the payments, SMS and EHR credentials are static per-clinic secrets (`payments.ts:33`). The SMS webhook also logs a failed signature check and carries on (`sms-webhook.ts:52`), so the delegated subject `phone:<from>` is unverified. |\n| A02 | gap | The audit schema requires all six fields. But the reminders `Halted` branch writes no audit record (`reminders.ts:49`), and pre-run refusals such as an invalid token write none either. Tenant also comes from the `x-clinic-id` header ahead of the verified JWT claim (`webchat.ts:43`). |\n| A03 | gap | The agent-type-id hash only reads `.txt` prompts (`identity.ts:24`), so `prompts/system.md`, the system prompt, is not hashed. Models are pinned snapshots, the ordering is fixed, and no secrets feed the hash. |\n| A04 | gap | The model's `input.clinicId` overrides the verified tenant (`executor.ts:63`) and is logged (`executor.ts:89`). The header-based clinic choice at `webchat.ts:44` is also used to look up the clinic. A04.3 passes: the subject is recorded separately from the agent identity. |\n| R14 | na_candidate | Nothing reads logs or checkpoints back for recovery, and there is no automatic replay. Audit goes write-only to Firehose and an object-locked S3 bucket. |\n\n- **Unknown checks:** A04.4 and the five R14 checks are `unknown`, with notes on where I looked. A04.4 is unknown because the repo has no queue producers. The approval handoff to the staff console carries no `traceparent`, and I couldn't tell whether that counts as a handoff.\n- **R14 evidence by hand:** `answer.py` only fills item-level evidence from a yes or no check. To satisfy the validator for R14, I added its evidence entry (`recorder.ts:54`) to the JSON by hand. That entry, `repo` and `scope` are the only hand edits.\n- **Prescan hits:** I resolved H006, as dismissed for A02.2 purposes only. The other prescan hits (H001–H005, H007–H011) belong to items outside this batch and are unresolved.\n- **A01.1 judgment call:** I answered yes. The reminders CronJob shares the `clinic-agent-runtime` role, but it runs the same agent image, so I treated it as part of the same agent.\n\nFiles are in `/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-ubni8w91/`:\n- `agent/brace-findings.json`\n- `agent/brace-prescan.json`\n- `agent/brace-inventory.json`\n- `work/` (my helper scripts and ledger inputs)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":948,"cache_read_input_tokens":99347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":948},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7a3da56-dd90-4bb0-a187-5c09c45dabd2","uuid":"bd88cb5a-5520-4f76-9f80-42f1d65c4f9b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:36:27.001Z","request_id":"req_011CgDjegEjABxBfbUKBTHP1"}
